# Owner: Tsegaye — Showcase Dashboard

You own the **screen the judges watch**. It shows the six tiles (2 crops × 3
markets) and updates live as agents enter data. This is where the pitch is won or
lost — it must look clean and it must visibly change when data comes in.

Read `000-project-overview.mdc` and `010-frontend-conventions.mdc` first.

## What you build

- `resources/js/Pages/Dashboard.tsx` — the page, route `GET /dashboard`.
- `resources/js/Components/PriceCard.tsx` — one tile per crop+market.
- `resources/js/Components/MarketMap.tsx` — Leaflet map of the three markets.
- `resources/js/Components/TrendChart.tsx` — small sparkline/trend per tile (use
  whatever chart lib the starter already has; don't add a second one).

## Data you consume (from Nba)

The page gets props from the controller — the six aggregated snapshots:

```ts
interface PriceSnapshot {
  crop: 'teff' | 'coffee';
  market: 'adama' | 'addis_ababa' | 'jimma';
  price: number;         // ETB / quintal — the aggregated number, not a raw report
  confidence: number;    // 0–100
  reportCount: number;
  lastUpdated: string;   // ISO
  trend: 'up' | 'down' | 'stable';
}
```

You do NOT compute prices or trends — Nba's engine does. You render what arrives.

## Live update (LOCKED: polling, not websockets)

Refresh on an interval so new agent entries appear within ~2–3s. With Inertia:

```tsx
import { router } from '@inertiajs/react';
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setInterval(() => router.reload({ only: ['snapshots'] }), 2500);
  return () => clearInterval(id);
}, []);
```

(Or Inertia v2 `usePoll(2500, { only: ['snapshots'] })` if available.) `only`
keeps it cheap — re-fetch just the snapshots prop, no full page reload. When a
tile's value changes, flash/animate it briefly so the change is *visible* on
stage — that reaction is the demo.

## Non-negotiable UI rule

**Never render a bare price.** Every `PriceCard` shows price **+ confidence % +
report count + last-updated**. That data-provenance stamp is the whole credibility
pitch (it proves the number is crowd-backed, not invented). A card with no
provenance is a bug.

- Trend arrows: `↑` green, `↓` red, `→` grey. Colors are relative to movement,
  not "good/bad".
- Low confidence (< ~40%) should look visibly different (muted / "collecting
  data") so the confidence story reads from across the room.

## Map

Leaflet, three markers (Adama, Addis Ababa, Jimma) using lat/long from the
`markets` table. Popup shows that market's current teff & coffee snapshot. Import
Leaflet CSS once; init in `useEffect`, clean up on unmount; never touch `window`
at module top level.

## Keep it demo-proof

Dashboard must render fine when data is thin (0–1 reports) — show "collecting
data / low confidence", never a crash or a blank tile.
